3. **Template:** pin 6S9K in the lead AlphaFold3 run, with an unpinned AlphaFold3 run alongside as a control.
4. **Unphosphorylated runs:** their models can go into the final five only if they pass the pocket gate.

The literature on this pair is thin. I found no paper on 14-3-3 binding LARP1 at Ser548, and I read only the abstracts of the two papers cited. I also don't have the organisers' description, so I can't confirm the peptide was phosphorylated in the experiment.

If nobody answers before the deadline, the brief says I take every recommended option and run the plan as written. That is about 300 models for roughly 5 GPU-h, capped at 20 of the 400 h budget.

